Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|testray.component.names|Site and Page Templates|
		|testray.main.component.name|Site and Page Templates|
	And these variables
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|testray.component.names|Site and Page Templates|
		|testray.main.component.name|Site and Page Templates|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance
	When User first Login PG
Teardown: This executes after each scenario 
	Given PortalInstances tear Down CP
		|testPortalInstance|TestPropsUtil#get('test.portal.instance')|
Scenario: Admin Can Not Add A Subpage Of A Child Page Linked To Site Template Page
Priority: 4
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	When SiteTemplates add CP
		|siteTemplateActive|Yes|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	And SiteTemplates add Site Page Via Site Template CP
		|pageName|Site Page Name|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	And SiteTemplates add Child Page Via Site Template CP
		|childSitepageName|true|
		|pageName|Site Page Name|
		|siteChildPageName|Site Child Page Name|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Site add Site Template CP
		|siteName|Site Name|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And SitePageNavigator goto Pages
		|page|Public Pages|
		|site|Site Name|
	Then Page view No Delete Pages Associated With Site Template
		|page|Site Child Page Name|
Scenario: Edit Site Template Guest Permissions
Priority: 4
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	When SiteTemplates add CP
		|siteTemplateName|${siteTemplateName}|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Site add Site Template CP
		|siteName|Site Name|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And PermissionsInline goto Site Template CP
		|page|home|
	And Role remove Permission PG
		|permissionDefinitionKey|CONTENT_PERMISSIONS_VIEW_CHECKBOX|
		|roleTitle|Guest|
	And Navigator goto Site Page
		|pageName|home|
		|siteName|Site Name|
	And PermissionsInline goto Site Template CP
		|page|home|
	Then Role define Permission PG
		|permissionDefinitionKey|CONTENT_PERMISSIONS_VIEW_CHECKBOX|
		|roleTitle|Guest|
Scenario: Portlet Preferences Persist With Site Template When Same Portlet Added On Second Page
Priority: 4
	Given TestCase get Site Name
##########################################################
The Poshi return element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
		|siteName|${siteName}|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	And SiteTemplates add CP
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	And Page add Page To Site Templates
		|pageName|Page1 Name|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	And SiteTemplatesNavigator goto Site Templates Page
		|pageName|Page1 Name|
		|siteName|${siteName}|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And Portlet add PG
		|defaultURL|false|
		|portletName|Hello World|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	And Page add Page To Site Templates
		|pageName|Page2 Name|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Site add Site Template CP
		|siteName|Site Name|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And Navigator goto Site Page
		|pageName|Page1 Name|
		|siteName|Site Name|
	And PermissionsInline goto Configuration PG
		|portletName|Hello World|
		|portletOption|Configuration|
	And Role remove Permission PG
		|permissionDefinitionKey|CONTENT_PERMISSIONS_VIEW_CHECKBOX|
		|roleTitle|Guest|
	And Refresh
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Site Templates|
	And SiteTemplates goto View Pages
		|siteName|${siteName}|
		|siteTemplateName|Site Template Name|
	And AssertClick the value 'Page2 Name' at locator 'Home#PAGE_TEMPLATE_3'
	And Portlet add PG
		|defaultURL|false|
		|portletName|Hello World|
	And Navigator goto Site Page
		|pageName|Page1 Name|
		|siteName|Site Name|
	And PermissionsInline goto Configuration PG
		|portletName|Hello World|
		|portletOption|Configuration|
	Then Role view Permission PG
		|permissionDefinitionKey|CONTENT_PERMISSIONS_VIEW_CHECKBOX|
		|permissionFlagged|false|
		|roleTitle|Guest|
Scenario: Site Admin Cannot Delete Pages That Were Created By Site Templates
